<quiz><question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Determining marriage rates for men and women</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Use the given data below to answer the questions that follow.</p>
<p>
<table border="solid">
  <tr>
    <th>Number of Marriages</th>
    <th>\({@no_marriages@}\)</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Total Population \(15+\)</td>
    <td>\({@total_popn@}\)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Total Female Population</td>
    <td>\({@females@}\)</td>
  </tr>
 
</table>
</p>
<br>
<p>Note: Leave your correct to \(2\) dp</p>
<p>Determine: </p>
<p>a). General marriage rate for women [[input:ans1]] \(‰\) [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>b). General marriage rate for men [[input:ans2]]  \(‰\) [[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p></p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>The general rates of marriage are determined as follows;</p>
<p>The General marriage rate for women </p>
<p>
\(\begin{align}
\text{GMR}^{f} \text{ per 1000}&=\displaystyle \frac{\text {total number of marriages}}{\text{Total female population}} \times 1000\\
&=\displaystyle \frac{{@no_marriages@}}{{@females@}} \times 1000\\
&={@gmr_females@} ‰\\
\end{align}\)
</p>
<p>The General marriage rate for men</p>
<p>
\(\begin{align}
\text{GMR}^{m} \text{ per 1000}&=\displaystyle \frac{\text {total number of marriages}}{\text{Total male population}} \times 1000\\
&=\displaystyle \frac{{@no_marriages@}}{{@men@}} \times 1000\\
&={@gmr_males@} ‰\\
\end{align}\)
</p>
<p></p>
<p></p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
